cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AgentProbe, please cite it as below."
title: "AgentProbe: Noise-aware evaluation and regression testing for AI agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yaragal
    given-names: Abhilash
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4892-6135"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24521435
repository-code: "https://github.com/abhilashyaragal570-del/agentprobe"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/agentprobe-eval/"
abstract: >-
  AgentProbe runs each test case for an AI agent several times, scores every
  run, labels cases as stable or flaky, and compares two reports with a
  Fisher exact test so that differences that could be chance are labelled
  NOISE instead of regressions. It excludes errored runs (rate limits,
  timeouts) from pass rates and includes a calculator for how many runs are
  needed to detect a drop of a given size.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - LLM evaluation
  - regression testing
  - flaky tests
  - statistical testing
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-17"